From: Bonesaw
Subject: [PATCH] Shadow Clone shows the owner's real character name

src/server/game/Handlers/QueryHandler.cpp -- one core-engine file, not
tracked in this repo (see modules/mod-living-gear/core-patches/README.md
for why and how to apply this).

WorldSession::HandleCreatureQueryOpcode is keyed by creature *template*
entry, not GUID, so every Shadow Clone (Living Gear's Rogue Subtlety pet,
entry 910201) normally shows the same static "Shadow Clone" name
regardless of who owns it. This special-cases that one entry to look up
the summon's real owner and substitute their actual character name.

Requires "Creature.h" and "ObjectAccessor.h" to be included in this file
(both are commonly already included in a stock AzerothCore checkout; add
them near the top if the build complains they're missing).

--- a/src/server/game/Handlers/QueryHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Handlers/QueryHandler.cpp
@@ -99,6 +99,15 @@
         Name = ci->Name;
         Title = ci->SubName;

+        // Living Gear's Subtlety "Shadow Clone" (entry 910201, mod-living-gear)
+        // is meant to be visually indistinguishable from the owning player --
+        // this query is keyed by template entry, not GUID, so every instance
+        // normally gets the same static "Shadow Clone" name from
+        // creature_template regardless of who owns it. Substitute the real
+        // owner's character name for this one entry only; falls straight
+        // through to the normal name on any lookup failure.
+        if (entry == 910201 && _player)
+            if (Creature* clone = ObjectAccessor::GetCreature(*_player, guid))
+                if (Unit* owner = clone->GetOwner())
+                    if (Player* ownerPlayer = owner->ToPlayer())
+                        Name = ownerPlayer->GetName();
+
         LocaleConstant loc_idx = GetSessionDbLocaleIndex();
         if (loc_idx >= 0)
         {
